# Models fetched by scripts/fetch_models.sh (zoo compile pinned by sha256).
# Vendored device artifacts in this directory (no rows here, kept via the
# .gitignore negation):
#   - yolo_world_v2s_540.hef — custom dual-input compile
#     (yolo_world_v2s/input_layer1 640x640x3 uint8 + input_layer2 80x512
#     uint16); no zoo equivalent.
#   - clip_vit_b_32_image_encoder_nv12.bin — AMPK package (app.yaml
#     spec.models path) exported from the platform model row via
#     platform-api `GET /api/v1/ai/models/:model_id/export`; the embedded
#     HEF bytes are identical to the vendored/zoo .hef, so the package
#     stays in sync with the artifact the app falls back to at runtime.
#     Regenerate after replacing the .hef (the package metadata pins the
#     HEF sha256).
# Zoo pinning rationale: v5.3.0/hailo15h matches the device firmware
# (HailoRT 5.3.0). The zoo clip compile is interface-identical to the device
# copy (input clip_vit_b_32_image_encoder/input_layer1 NV12 112x224x3, output
# conv50 NHWC 1x1x512 — verified with hailortcli parse-hef), and vocabulary
# embeddings are always self-generated with the active encoder, so a fresh
# device can boot from the zoo artifact and re-index on startup.
ecbf4a201272548c8d5a33a30ab138c7a95bad68e15f7196aa4c2458fa7d02d6	clip_vit_b_32_image_encoder_nv12.hef	https://hailo-model-zoo.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/ModelZoo/Compiled/v5.3.0/hailo15h/clip_vit_b_32_image_encoder_nv12.hef
